"tgtext": "Users Report Deposit Restrictions at OKX, Binance and Other Exchanges Following FinCEN Action Against MEXC\n\nFollowing the U.S. Treasury\u2019s Financial Crimes Enforcement Network (FinCEN) issuance of a special measure order targeting MEXC Global, some community users reported that funds withdrawn from MEXC to centralized exchanges, including OKX, Binance, and Gate, were subjected to compliance reviews, held pending deposit crediting, or placed under refund review by the receiving platforms. Separately, Bitget Wallet confirmed that its card top-up service currently does not accept funds identified as originating from MEXC. FinCEN\u2019s order has not yet taken effect. The exchange-related reports are primarily based on individual user accounts rather than official platform-wide restriction announcements. The scope of any restrictions and the eventual disposition of affected funds remain unclear. \u2014 link",
"title": "Users Report Deposit Restrictions at OKX, Binance and Other Exchanges Following FinCEN Action Against MEXC",
"url": "https://t.me/wublockchainenglish/26728",
"urls": []
},
